Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3-msm: find available controller child by compatible

Base kernel:6bde5fc06b252c97761bc0963dd13c1abcf377ab.
The first available child can be a different device, such as qcom,usbbam.
Select an available snps,dwc3 child regardless of the device-tree ordering.
The iterator releases skipped children; breaking retains the matching node
for the existing of_node_put paths after population or on population error.
No shutdown, logging, clock, PHY or deferred-probe behavior is changed.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm.c
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm.c
@@ -3919,6 +3919,9 @@ static int dwc3_msm_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
-	/* Assumes dwc3 is the first DT child of dwc3-msm */
-	dwc3_node = of_get_next_available_child(node, NULL);
+	/* Find the available DWC3 controller independently of DT ordering. */
+	for_each_available_child_of_node(node, dwc3_node) {
+		if (of_device_is_compatible(dwc3_node, "snps,dwc3"))
+			break;
+	}
 	if (!dwc3_node) {
 		dev_err(&pdev->dev, "failed to find dwc3 child\n");
 		ret = -ENODEV;
 		goto err;
